title: The First Congress of the <span style="color: var(--dvp-colour);">Deutsche Volkspartei</span>.
subtitle: The DVP clarifies its course..
new-page: true
view-if: year = 1919 and month = 4 and weeks = 2
max-visits: 1
tags: event

The DVP was formed after talks of a united <span style="color: var(--lvp-colour);">liberal</span> party collapsed in early winter 1918, being made of whatever is left of the <span class="wide_tooltip-wrap drop-down"><span style="color: var(--nlp-colour);">Nationalliberale Partei</span><span class="wide_tooltip-tip"><img src="img/logo_nlp.webp">The <span style="color: var(--nlp-colour);">**NLP**</span> was a party which was active during the times of the Empire, however it dissolved in 1918 with much of its left-wing going to us.</span></span> from the Empire. This has subsequently caused a virtual collapse of their support and in party organization in past <span style="color: var(--nlp-colour);">**NLP**</span> strongholds. If it wasn't for their chairman, Gustav Stresemann's ability to rally the party in the west, the party would surely have faced a humiliating defeat in the National Assembly.

Despite trying to portrait themselves as a "<span style="color: var(--dvp-colour);">People's Party</span>", the DVP are still clearly dominated by professional politicians, senior civil servants and industrial representatives as has been shown in the National Assembly, where there is a notable absence of working-class DVP deputies.

Although Stresemann has shown sympathies towards <span style="color: var(--dnvp-colour);">nationalist</span> and <span style="color: var(--i-colour);">monarchist</span> ideals, as he has sent a congratulatory birthday telegram to the exiled Kaiser with two other members of his party, the DVP as a whole has revolted and has forced him to tentatively support the current order. Over the course of the coming months, his position has further moderated, mostly due to the new constitution satisfying most of the goals that the old <span style="color: var(--nlp-colour);">**NLP**</span> had being trying to achieve and also partly due to the National Assembly Of German-Austria approving the <span class="wide_tooltip-wrap">Anschluss<span class="wide_tooltip-tip"><img src="img/anschluss.jpeg">The "Anschluss" is the idea of a union between Germany and Austria, one that many <span style="color: var(--dnvp-colour);">nationalists</span> seek due to both countries having similar culture.</span></span>.
